    {
      "id": "page_0000",
      "title": "The two chambers",
      "text_script": {
        "pointer_type": "String Constant",
        "script_element_type": "Pointer",
        "value": "\"One chamber holds the missing ration,\" Mara says. \"West belongs to the orbit that settles at one. East belongs to the orbit that cycles through five and seven.\" A sealed mechanism began at either one or five, with equal chance. Its current lamp reads one modulo four in both cases. Each tick adds thirteen; a state equal to one modulo four is first tripled. The mechanism then removes every factor of two. Sampling the next lamp costs one eighth of a ration. Amber means one modulo four; blue means three. A preserved arithmetic seal is free to read. Your score is the recovered ration, if any, less the sample cost."
      },
      "earliest_turn": 0,
      "latest_turn": 99,
      "acceptability_script": true,
      "creation_index": 0,
